'' A 'ustring * N' ARGUMENT WAS NOT A FIXED STRING AT ALL, and then it was passed raw.
''
'' TWO BUGS, one on each side of the call. FixedStringElem listed TY_ZSTRING, TY_WSTRING,
'' TY_USTRING and TY_FIXSTR and NOT TY_FIXUSTR, so StrFlavourOf_'s own TY_FIXUSTR arm
'' could never be reached and every 'ustring * N' argument cost CONV_NONE against a
'' 'ustring' parameter. The call bound to nothing, came out UNTYPED, and whatever
'' consumed it declined. The narrow twin was listed and worked, which is what kept it
'' invisible.
''
'' And where the call did go out -- as a bare statement, where nothing consumes the
'' result -- tiko-lang passed '@uf', the raw uint16 buffer, where an FBUSTRING* belongs:
'' the callee read the first eight bytes of the TEXT as a data pointer. It lowered and
'' it verified.
''
'' The copy-out is emitted whether or not the parameter is CONST, which is what fbc
'' does. A const parameter makes it a no-op, and guessing which is which would be a
'' semantic fork over an observable write.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/ustring-fixed-arg.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z1GRK8FBSTRING
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z1GRK9FBUSTRING
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrDelete
'' GOLDEN: expected/ustring-fixed-arg.out
